## 1. STRICT RULES & ARCHITECTURE

**1.1 CSS-First Architecture & Zero Inline CSS**
- All styling lives in `style.css`. **Forbidden:** the `style="..."` attribute anywhere in the HTML.
- Target every design property, layout rule, and state via class or ID selectors only.
- HTML must remain clean, semantic, and styling-agnostic: reskinning the page must require editing only `style.css`, never the markup.

**1.2 CSS Variables & Theme Tokens**
- Consume only the tokens above — no hard-coded hex values, sizes, or shadows outside `:root` and the dark-mode override block.
- **Contrast pairing:** every light background token pairs with a dark text token and every dark background token pairs with a light text token — enforce the pairing in every theme, not just the default.
- All radii, shadows, spacing, transitions, easing, and stacking contexts must reference the tokens (`--z-dropdown` for the mobile nav panel, `--z-toast` for any toast).

**1.3 Mandatory Dark Mode Support**
- The source spec declares no modes ("source does not declare modes; validate in light and dark before publishing") — therefore you **must derive and ship a dark theme**: invert the warm ink-and-paper character (paper → warm near-black, ink → warm off-white). Suggested starting point, to be validated at WCAG AA before publishing:

```css
.dark {
  --color-bg: #16130e; --color-surface: #1f1a13; --color-surface-strong: #292217;
  --color-border: #463c2d; --color-text: #f2ede3; --color-text-muted: #b4a88f;
  --color-primary: #d06a4d;   /* lightened for text/borders on dark; keep #8a2a1e for filled buttons with light text */
  --color-accent: #7fb5ad;
  --text-success: #8fc7a6; --text-error: #e58877;
}
```
- Implement via a `.dark` class on `<html>` **and** `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root:not(.light) { … } }` so first visits with no stored preference follow the OS. Background/text variables must swap seamlessly with zero HTML restructuring.
- **Persistence:** store the choice in `localStorage` (fall back to `prefers-color-scheme` on first visit); applying the stored theme must be the first action of `script.js`. Provide a visible toggle in the nav with correct `aria-pressed` and a dynamic `aria-label` ("Switch to dark theme" / "Switch to light theme").
- Adjust shadow alpha for dark surfaces so elevation remains perceptible.

**1.4 Flexbox Layout & Mobile-First Alignment**
- Build all layout structures with Flexbox (and CSS Grid for multi-column editorial spreads).
- **Every flex container defaults to `align-items: center`** unless there is an explicitly justified exception (e.g., `align-items: stretch` for equal-height card columns — document each exception with a CSS comment).
- Mobile-first: rows collapse to columns below ~768px; use `clamp()` for display type; **horizontal scrolling is forbidden at any viewport width down to 320px**.

**1.5 Styling Approach (Framework Default)**
- The provided token system and base classes are the canonical design system. Write clean custom CSS; Tailwind CSS is permitted only if every utility maps back to these variables/classes via `@layer`/`@apply`. Never mix conventions.

**1.6 Typography & Icons (Google Fonts Mandatory)**
- Load **Playfair Display** (400/700/900 + italic), **Inter**, and **IBM Plex Mono** via Google Fonts `<link>` tags with `preconnect`; bind them to `--font-display`, `--font-sans`/`--font-base`, and `--font-mono` per the token block.
- Icons: **Google Material Symbols (Outlined)** via Google Fonts. **Explicitly forbidden:** raw inline SVGs and local icon files. Required icon usage: theme toggle (`dark_mode`/`light_mode`), FAQ chevron (`expand_more`), form validity (`check_circle`/`error`), feature glyphs, back-to-top (`arrow_upward`). Material Symbols has no brand glyphs — render social links as mono uppercase text links.

