## 4. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

- **Responsive by default:** fluid `clamp()` type, container max-width ≈72rem, prose measure ≈65ch, `max-width: 100%` imagery, zero horizontal overflow at 320px.
- **Smooth animations:** `transition: var(--transition-normal) var(--ease-standard)` on all state changes; honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (disable transforms, shimmer, smooth scroll; accordions become instant). Any scroll-reveal must be progressive enhancement — content fully visible without JS.
- **Accessibility (a11y):** WCAG AA contrast in **both** light and dark modes; never communicate state by color alone; semantic HTML5 landmarks (`header`/`nav`/`main`/`section`/`footer`), one `h1`, logical heading order, logical DOM/focus order, full keyboard operability, visible `:focus-visible` rings, correct ARIA on the accordion, nav panel, theme toggle, and billing toggle; `aria-live` regions for form feedback and dynamic updates.
- **Mandatory visual feedback:** every click, hover, focus, and submission triggers a visible state change.
- **Luxury restraint:** generous `--space-16`/`--space-24` section rhythm, fine 1px rules, letter-spaced mono kickers, restrained shadows — no gaudy effects.

